any
opinion @1 city against 1 : A #city# #merchant# sells #iron# with a bright #label# and no name I know. | I prefer the local #forge#.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #festival# brings every #neighbour# past my #counter#. | The #forge# can cool for an evening.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A #merchant# brings #iron# I cannot make here. | I still count the #cost# before setting a #price#.
opinion @1 road against 1 : A late #wagon# leaves an #order# on my #bench# without its #iron#. | I can find a better #path# through the #bog#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger# may need a #shoe# fitted before speaking of home. | I ask the work first.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #coal# costs more every season. | I cannot keep the #forge# hot on yesterday's #coin#.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : The #watch# passes my #door# when the #shop# closes. | I still lock the #stock# away.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A great #house# has #hinges# like any cottage. | I charge for the #iron# and the #hands# who shape it.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : A fresh #hand# can begin at the #bellows#. | I watch where they stand near the #fire#.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Have you brought a #tool# or a question? | #greet#. The #forge# is taking #heat#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I have #stew# upstairs for later. | Come see the #trap# I mended.
line @1 greet.return : The #shoe# is cooler now. | You returned before I finished that #hinge#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #coals# have just woken. | The #river# may be clear this #morning#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come upstairs when the #forge# settles. | A #plate# waits beside the upstairs #window#.
line @1 again.open : I was explaining the #edge#. | Was that the #bog# crossing you meant?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #anvil# is waiting. | Mind the #mud# past the #door#.
line @1 farewell.return : Bring the #tool# back if it loosens. | I may have #eels# by then.
line @1 react.news : Say it while I set this #bar# down. | Did a #traveller# bring the account?
line @1 react.news.new : The #smithy# has heard none of that. | Who brought it to #market#?
line @1 react.news.known : A #buyer# gave me the short version. | Yours has a different bend.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would inspect the #tool# before agreeing. | Which #hand# saw the #tool# fail in use?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Come away from the #forge#. | I can leave the #iron# until later.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. There will be #stew# enough tonight. | I might put the #hammer# down for that.
line @1 answer.how : The #forge# held its #heat#; the #river# gave me an #eel#. | Better after a warm #day#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am fitting this #shoe# to the #anvil#. | Let me quench the #bar# first.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# bring you over dry ground? | Have you seen the #river# this week?
line @1 sympathise : The end of this #bench# is clear of #sparks#. | Once the #fire# settles, I can serve you #stew#.
line @1 reassure : A cracked #shoe# can be made sound again. | There is a firm #path# around the #bog#.
line @1 decline : I will not hand over #iron# while it is hot. | That #trap# needs more than one #nail#.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand; the #order# stays on the #bench#. | That #tool# may stay on the #bench# for now.
line @1 thank : You worked the #bellows# evenly for me. | That #stew# was welcome after the #river#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had the #tongs# ready. | The #eel# found the #trap# on its own.
line @1 preclose : I should bank the #coals# before #night#. | The #trap# line needs a look.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #hammer# aim could find any #bog# #path#. | That #eel# would have escaped a slower #trap#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #edge# is straight. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #price#.
line @1 give.advice : Let the #bar# reach even #heat# before the first #blow#. | Set an #eel# #trap# where the #current# turns.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Take company on the #road# after #nightfall#. | Keep the #wagon# near the #watch#.
scene forge_heat
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #bar# in one part of the #fire# until its color is even. | A bright end and dark middle will bend badly.
b : Can you see it clearly? | Who tends the coals?
a : Under the #roof#. | We take turns.

scene shoe_curve
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #shoe# must match the hoof before I set the #nails#. | I shape it twice rather than force a poor fit.
b : Does that take long? | Do you fit many?
a : Less than a lame horse. | Enough in a season.

scene anvil_face
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #anvil# face clear of stray #shavings# and #ash#. | A small speck can mark hot #iron#.
b : Do you wipe it often? | Does that matter?
a : Between #orders#. | For a fine #edge#.

scene hinge_pin
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #hinge# can fail at the pin before the plate shows wear. | I turn it in my #hand# before heating anything.
b : Can you mend it? | Do people notice?
a : Usually. | When the #door# sags.

scene bellows_rhythm
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A steady #bellows# stroke keeps the #coals# ready without throwing #sparks#. | I show a new #hand# the rhythm first.
b : Do they learn quickly? | Who taught you?
a : After a few tries. | An older smith.

scene quench_bucket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bucket# water warms through a long #day#. | I change it before a delicate #blade# goes in.
b : Does warm water matter? | Where do you fetch more?
a : For the #edge#. | From the pump.

scene farm_tool
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #tool# from the #field# tells me how its owner holds it. | I leave the worn #wood# where the #hand# expects it.
b : Do you replace any part? | Can you tell its age?
a : Only what is cracked. | From its #marks#.

scene iron_order
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I write each #order# beside the #cost# of #coal# and #iron#. | The #price# should be clear before I light the #forge#.
b : Do people bargain? | Does the price change?
a : Sometimes. | With the #wagon#.

scene late_iron
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #wagon# brought a load of #bars# after the #fire# had gone out. | I checked the #stock# at #morning# instead.
b : Was it sound? | Did the driver wait?
a : Most of it. | Until the count.

scene bog_path
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can cross the low #bog# by following the firmer #reeds#. | The #road# goes farther around.
b : Is that safe? | Do you guide others?
a : After I test it. | When they listen.

scene river_trap
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The best #trap# sits where the #river# #current# bends. | I check its #line# before the #day# warms.
b : Do you catch many? | Who taught you?
a : More than I tell the #market#. | The #river# did.

scene eel_boast
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have pulled an #eel# from a #trap# others called empty. | They had set it where the #water# ran straight.
b : Did you show them? | Do you always win?
a : After I ate. | I know where to look.

scene trap_repair
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A broken #trap# takes a finer #hand# than a #shoe#. | I mend the #line# beside the #fire# after work.
b : Do you use iron? | When will it need mending again?
a : Only a small #hinge#. | Until the next #flood#.

scene whittled_handle
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I whittle a new #wood# handle when the #forge# is quiet. | A #knife# and steady light are enough.
b : Who uses it? | Do you sell them?
a : The #hand# with a worn #tool#. | Only with the tool.

scene mutton_stew
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #pot# of #mutton# #stew# is better after a cold #river# morning. | I keep a #plate# upstairs for the late #hand#.
b : Do you cook it? | Does it last?
a : When I have time. | Until supper.

scene tidy_flat
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave the #smithy# #floor# swept before climbing to the #flat#. | A tidy #home# gives the #forge# a proper end.
b : Do you live alone? | Does it stay tidy?
a : Most nights. | Until another #order#.

scene first_warm_day
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first warm #day# of #spring# sends me to the #river# before the #market#. | The #eels# move differently then.
b : Do you still open the shop? | Does it feel warmer?
a : After the traps. | At the #bank#.

scene stale_loaf
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A stale #loaf# makes poor supper after a hard #day#. | I put it in the #stew# rather than waste it.
b : Does that help? | Do you buy fresh?
a : It softens. | When the baker has it.

scene bad_manners
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #customer# once reached for hot #iron# after I warned them. | I closed the #tongs# and made them wait.
b : Were they angry? | Did they learn?
a : For a moment. | They kept their #hands#.

scene river_flood
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #flood# can carry every #trap# past the #bank# overnight. | I pull the #lines# before heavy #rain#.
b : Have you lost any? | Can you find them?
a : Two. | Not in that #current#.

scene new_striker
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A young #striker# watches the #hammer# head more than the hot #bar#. | I tell them to watch both #hands#.
b : Do they improve? | Do you trust them?
a : With a #lesson#. | Once they can stop.

scene market_repair
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At the #market# someone always brings a #hinge# that broke at dawn. | I ask how the #door# was hung before pricing it.
b : Does that change the repair? | Do they answer?
a : Often. | After a little thought.

scene watch_shoe
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #watch# brings worn #shoes# for its mounts. | I fit them the same as any farm animal.
b : Do they pay promptly? | Are the horses calm?
a : When the #book# is right. | Most are.

scene coal_count
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Before hearing the #merchant# #price#, I weigh the #coal#. | The #forge# cannot run on a light #sack#.
b : Do they object? | Can you weigh it?
a : If it is short. | On the #scale#.

scene quiet_evening
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After the last #order#, I sit upstairs and trim a piece of #wood#. | The #river# can wait until #morning#.
b : Do you rest then? | Do you think of work?
a : For a while. | Only when a #tool# is unfinished.

scene river_reeds
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Tall #reeds# mark the dry edge of a #bog# better than a painted sign. | I walk where their roots hold.
b : Do they move after rain? | Can I follow?
a : Sometimes. | If you watch the ground.

scene last_spark
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I check the last #spark# before shutting the #smithy# #door#. | The #coals# must be banked before I leave.
b : How do you know? | Does anyone check too?
a : The #heat# falls. | The #striker# does.

story first_shoe [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : My first #shoe# looked even on the #anvil# and crooked on the hoof.
  : I heated it again rather than force the #nails#.
  ask : Did it fit then?
  b : A good correction.
  : After another careful #blow#.

story river_turn [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I set a #trap# where the #river# bends against the #reeds#.
  : At dawn it held an #eel# larger than the others expected.
  b : That water's yours by now. Did you tell them?
  : Often enough that they know my claim.

story bog_shortcut [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : A #cart# took the long #road# while I crossed the #bog# on foot.
  : I arrived before its #wheel# reached the #bridge#.
  ask : Was the ground safe?
  b : A useful path.
  : I tested each step.

story flooded_trap [topic=weather self.age>=18]
  : A #flood# rose while my #traps# were still tied at the #bank#.
  : I pulled the #lines# before the water took them.
  b : A close call. Did you save them all?
  : All but one broken frame.

story warm_spring [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : The first warm #day# drew me to the #river# after the #forge# closed.
  : I found the #eels# moving beneath a new bank of #reeds#.
  ask : Did the shop wait?
  b : A good day to go.
  : The #orders# were finished first.

rule @bark_forge
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #bar# has even #heat#. | Keep the #sparks# off the #bench#.

rule @bark_shoe
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say This #shoe# needs another curve. | Hold the #tongs# steady.

rule @bark_trap
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #river# #line# is ready. | There may be an #eel# by dawn.

rule @bark_bog
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #reeds# show firm ground. | That #path# crosses the #bog#.

rule @bark_stew
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The #stew# smells ready. | I will bring a #plate# upstairs.

rule @bark_closing
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 13h
say Bank the #coals# carefully. | The last #order# is in the #book#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #forge# is hot. | #greet#. Have you come for #iron# or #eels#?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Your last #order# is still on the #bench#. | The #river# gave me another #eel#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The #coals# are banked for #night#. | I am upstairs; come back at #morning#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I run the #forge# at #self.workplace#. | I fit #shoes#, mend #tools#, and keep the #orders#.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.working=yes] : This #bar# needs a careful #strike#. | I am fitting a #shoe# before it cools.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will close the #smithy#. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the #sparks#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. Each #tool# on that #shelf# has a marked #price#. | Tell me what needs mending.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Finished #iron# is scarce today. | Name the #tool# you seek; I will mark the next #forge# run.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The #forge# is resting. | Come when the #coals# are hot again.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. I can inspect your #tool# here. | The #counter# is open for new #orders#.
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open|bare] : The #price# covers #iron#, #coal#, and the #hands# shaping it. | I mark each #cost# before work starts.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Let the #iron# cool before carrying it. | #shop_bye# I have another #order# to finish.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Start by keeping the #bellows# even. | Stand beside me and watch the #sparks# clear of the #forge#.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=yes topic.meeting=known] : Your last #strike# was true. | Today you can shape a small #nail#.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you cross any bog? -> bog
node bog
say I follow the #reeds# and test each #step# before trusting it.
free
choice Are you really the best eel trapper? -> eel
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node eel
say I know where the #current# bends. You may ask anyone on the #river#.
choice Back to the forge. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Can you mend this tool? -> tool
node tool
say Let me see its #edge# and #handle# before I name a #price#.
free
choice When will it be ready? -> ready
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node ready
say Your #tool# goes on my #order# list; I will name a day for the #forge#.
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #anvil# is clear. | #greet#. The #river# is low today.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will bank the #coals#. | The #traps# can wait until dawn.
